<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  The hardened runtime's entitlements for fleetd.app: none. Each exception it could ask for, and why it doesn't:
  - cs.allow-jit, cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory: no JIT. Metal compiles gpui's shaders in Apple's own
    compiler service, not in this process.
  - cs.disable-library-validation: the app loads only system frameworks; everything else is linked in statically.
  - cs.allow-dyld-environment-variables: nothing relies on DYLD_* variables.
  - device.camera, device.audio-input, automation.apple-events: the app uses none of them. Recording its own
    window (FLEETD_RECORD) needs Screen Recording consent, which has no entitlement.
  - Network, notifications and the login keychain need no entitlement outside the App Sandbox, which the app
    doesn't use.
  The key store check in the release dry run launches the signed app and has it dial a hub, so a missing exception
  shows up there, not on someone's Mac.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict/>
</plist>
